Java's String class provides many built-in methods for creating, comparing, searching, and manipulating strings. Here are the most commonly used ones:
Method
Description
Example
length()
Returns the length of the string
"Java".length() → 4
charAt(int index)
Returns the character at the specified index
"Java".charAt(1) → 'a'
substring(int beginIndex)
Returns substring from the given index
"Java".substring(2) → "va"
substring(int begin, int end)
Returns substring between indices
"Java".substring(1,3) → "av"
toUpperCase()
Converts to uppercase
"java".toUpperCase() → "JAVA"
toLowerCase()
Converts to lowercase
"JAVA".toLowerCase() → "java"
trim()
Removes leading and trailing spaces
" Hello ".trim() → "Hello"
isEmpty()
Checks if string is empty
"".isEmpty() → true
isBlank()
Checks if string contains only whitespace
"   ".isBlank() → true
equals(String)
Compares two strings
"Java".equals("Java") → true
equalsIgnoreCase(String)
Compares ignoring case
"java".equalsIgnoreCase("JAVA") → true
compareTo(String)
Lexicographically compares strings
"abc".compareTo("abd") → -1
contains(CharSequence)
Checks if substring exists
"Java".contains("av") → true
startsWith(String)
Checks prefix
"Java".startsWith("Ja") → true
endsWith(String)
Checks suffix
"Java".endsWith("va") → true
indexOf(String)
Returns first occurrence index
"Java".indexOf("a") → 1
lastIndexOf(String)
Returns last occurrence index
"Java".lastIndexOf("a") → 3
replace(old, new)
Replaces characters or substrings
"Java".replace("a","o") → "Jovo"
replaceAll(regex, replacement)
Replaces using regular expression
"a1b2".replaceAll("\\d","") → "ab"
split(String regex)
Splits string into an array
"a,b,c".split(",")
concat(String)
Concatenates strings
"Hello".concat(" World") → "Hello World"
valueOf()
Converts other data types to string
String.valueOf(100) → "100"
join(delimiter, elements)
Joins strings
String.join("-", "A","B","C") → "A-B-C"
repeat(int count)
Repeats the string
"Hi".repeat(3) → "HiHiHi"
Example Program
public class StringMethodsDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String str = " Hello Java ";

        System.out.println(str.length());                // 12
        System.out.println(str.trim());                  // Hello Java
        System.out.println(str.toUpperCase());           // HELLO JAVA
        System.out.println(str.toLowerCase());           // hello java
        System.out.println(str.contains("Java"));        // true
        System.out.println(str.substring(7));            // Java
        System.out.println(str.replace("Java", "World"));// Hello World
        System.out.println(str.startsWith(" "));         // true
        System.out.println(str.endsWith(" "));           // true
    }
}
